  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Malayenolide C interacts with the DNA polymerase iota enzyme, which in turn targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, with Malayenolide C being a common target for DNA polymerase iota across different compounds, including Macaflavone II and CID 53630653. These compounds, though distinct, share the same target pathway, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The scores from the pathways suggest a moderate level of confidence in this interaction, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence highlights a possible role for Malayenolide C in modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through its interaction with DNA polymerase iota, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanisms involved.",
